{%- comment -%}
  WALLY DOMO: the CTA style from Dawn (Marc, 2026-10-07; carried to Horizon 2026-10-22).
  2px stroke, no fill, label in the CTA colour. Hover / keyboard focus fills it with that
  colour and a near-white label, so the click still feels like a button. Disabled
  (sold out) never fills. Every other button stays a solid fill.

  The CTA colour is the button's own border colour, so the editor still drives it:
    - Our homepage series buttons (Button style "Custom") = the series colour.
    - Add to cart and Checkout = Theme settings > Colors > Primary button border (ink).
  Utility for custom liquid: class "wd-cta" on any .button.
  Rendered from snippets/wd-fonts.liquid (our file).
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  html body :is(.button-custom, .add-to-cart-button, .cart__checkout-button, .button.wd-cta):not(.button-unstyled) {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: var(--button-border-color) !important;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--button-border-color) !important;
    transition: background-color .15s ease, color .15s ease, box-shadow .15s ease;
  }
  html body :is(.button-custom, .add-to-cart-button, .cart__checkout-button, .button.wd-cta):not(.button-unstyled):not([disabled], [aria-disabled='true']):is(:hover, :focus-visible) {
    background-color: var(--button-background-color) !important;
    color: var(--button-color) !important;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--button-background-color) !important;
  }
  html body :is(.button-custom, .add-to-cart-button, .cart__checkout-button, .button.wd-cta) svg { color: currentColor; }
</style>
